Whisper: app identity (vendor name, Firefox User-Agent, --version)

What: sets the application vendor to Whisper, keeps "Firefox" as the application name
in the User-Agent string, and makes --version print "Whisper 159.0.1" instead of
"Whisper Whisper 159.0.1".
Why: these values can only be set by the build project (browser/moz.configure), not
from a mozconfig. With the vendor set to Whisper, Whisper keeps its profiles in its own
folder and never opens a Firefox profile. The User-Agent stays exactly Firefox's, so
web pages cannot tell Whisper apart from Firefox of the same version by it.
Adapted from: LibreWolf's moz-configure.patch, firefox-in-UA.patch and the --version
part of vendor-name.patch (MPL-2.0).
---
diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
index 8979a2e4e8..055df85e58 100644
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -11,7 +11,9 @@ imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)
 
 
-imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Mozilla")
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Whisper")
+# Web pages and servers see the same User-Agent as Firefox of this version.
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_UA_NAME", "Firefox")
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_ID", "{ec8030f7-c20a-464f-9b0e-13a3a9e97384}")
 # Include the DevTools client, not just the server (which is the default)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEVTOOLS", "all")
diff --git a/toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp b/toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp
index 003fc8545a..fdf8bcc141 100644
--- a/toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp
+++ b/toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp
@@ -2250,9 +2250,6 @@ static void DumpHelp() {
 }
 
 static inline void DumpVersion() {
-  if (gAppData->vendor && *gAppData->vendor) {
-    printf("%s ", (const char*)gAppData->vendor);
-  }
   printf("%s ", (const char*)gAppData->name);
 
   // Use the displayed version
@@ -2266,9 +2263,6 @@ static inline void DumpVersion() {
 }
 
 static inline void DumpFullVersion() {
-  if (gAppData->vendor && *gAppData->vendor) {
-    printf("%s ", (const char*)gAppData->vendor);
-  }
   printf("%s ", (const char*)gAppData->name);
 
   // Use the displayed version
